1 workflow run: steps = N total entries).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.07,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["`| ci_gate | scripts/check_*.py glob, plus workflow run: steps | 29 / 251 |`","Every other row (lock 26, env_var 132, config_key 76, feature_flag 27, autouse_fixture 145, test_helper 19) shows exactly one count."],"finding":"The `ci_gate` row in the live-counts table shows `29 / 251` — a two-number notation unique to that row, with no explanation of what 251 denotes or which number the baseline locks. Every other kind shows a single count. Since AC3 requires zero false positives against a clean tree and the baseline is 'locked to counts at introduction', the ci_gate count is ambiguous.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa499463726271f33","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — live counts table, `ci_gate` row","norm_id":"n1c65ce5bcaf48d5c","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor cannot determine the expected ci_gate baseline entry count, so AC3's 'zero false positives' target for this kind is unverifiable."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace `29 / 251` with an explicit total and breakdown, e.g. `280 (29 check_*.py + 251 workflow run: steps)`, matching the single-count form the other rows use for baseline locking.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify where the '# mechanism-ok: <kind> <name> — <reason>' marker attaches (and which lines each detector scans for it) for the filename-glob and YAML-derived kinds — ci_gate (scripts/check_*.py, workflow run: steps) and test_helper (tests/_*.py) — not only for the AST/config kinds that have a natural definition line.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.07,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'A new mechanism may be admitted by an inline comment at its definition site'","Plan detection table: ci_gate = 'scripts/check_*.py glob, plus workflow run: steps'; test_helper = 'tests/_*.py glob' — a filename glob has no single definition line the way an AST ClassDef or a _SECTIONS entry does","Precedent check_config_reads.py binds '# read-via:' to the field line or the immediately preceding line (lines 103-119) — a discipline available only because the field IS a line; the plan inherits the pattern but not a rule for glob/YAML-derived kinds"],"finding":"The '# mechanism-ok:' marker is specified only as an inline comment 'at its definition site' scanned during the per-state pass, but three of the seven kinds are detected without a natural single definition line: ci_gate (scripts/check_*.py filename glob + workflow run: steps) and test_helper (tests/_*.py filename glob). The plan does not state where a marker attaches for a filename-glob-detected mechanism (e.g. a new scripts/check_foo.py) or for a YAML run: step, nor which lines each detector scans for markers, leaving the justified-exception path (AC5) ambiguous or unusable for those kinds.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f03ad34fded968273","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'The justified-exception path is an in-tree marker' paragraph; AC5","norm_id":"nc9911c1f21a2e9b4","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A contributor adds a new scripts/check_foo.py gate (a new ci_gate entry by glob) and needs to justify it, but there is no specified line the marker must occupy for detect_ci to associate it","A new workflow run: step is added and the reviewer must decide whether the marker goes on the step, the job, or a preceding YAML comment"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"For filename-glob kinds, define the marker site as a top-of-file comment in the matched file (e.g. within the first N lines of scripts/check_foo.py / tests/_foo.py); for workflow run: steps, define it as a '# mechanism-ok:' comment on or immediately preceding the step. State that detect_ci/detect_code scan those specific locations, and add a per-kind AC4/AC5 case covering a glob-detected and a YAML-detected mechanism.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the `name` derivation rule for each detector — in particular how a workflow `run:` step and a `check_*.py` glob hit map to a stable, unique `name` component of the `(kind, name)` key.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["`ci_gate | scripts/check_*.py glob, plus workflow run: steps` — the name for a run: step is unspecified.","Baseline key shape is `<kind>::<name>` and AC1 asserts name-set disjointness, so `name` must be deterministic per site.","Lock names are described (ClassDef / `\\.lock$` literal) but ci_gate step names are not."],"finding":"For the `ci_gate` and `feature_flag`/`config_key` detectors the derivation of the per-entry `name` is left implicit. The disjointness assertion (AC1) and the `(kind, name)` baseline key both depend on a well-defined `name` per detected site, but the plan does not state how a workflow `run:` step or a boolean `_SECTIONS` key maps to its `name` string.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f90432f972495a97e","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — seven-kinds table and partition discussion; AC1","norm_id":"n3e7279a62fd914ea","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two workflow run: steps with identical commands could collide to one baseline key, or an unstable name (line number, step index) could churn the baseline across unrelated edits."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a one-line name rule per detector, e.g. ci_gate name = script basename for check_*.py, and `<workflow>:<job>:<step-name>` for run: steps (falling back to a stable hash of the command when the step is unnamed).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"