blind spot — rather than citing ESLint as the precedent for 'never a scalar sum'.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Retrieved ESLint docs (eslint.org/docs/latest/use/suppressions) and DeepWiki: the suppressions file stores 'suppression counts per file and per rule'.","Retrieved GitHub issue eslint/eslint#21226: 'The suppressions file (eslint-suppressions.json) records a count per (file, rule), not per specific violation' — and flags a same-count-swap blind spot within a bucket.","Plan text asserts its baseline is 'never a scalar sum — per the ESLint eslint-suppressions.json shape', but ESLint's shape IS a scalar count within each (file,rule) bucket."],"finding":"The external prior-art citation to ESLint's eslint-suppressions.json is inverted: ESLint's format records a scalar COUNT per (file, rule) bucket, so citing it as precedent for 'never a scalar sum' misrepresents the source.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8b3d61895cf8515b","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context section: 'Baseline keyed per (kind, name) — never a scalar sum — per the ESLint eslint-suppressions.json shape (12c)'","norm_id":"n422f5e3bbdf9b07d","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or future maintainer checks the cited ESLint format and finds it is scalar-per-bucket, undermining confidence in the plan's prior-art grounding.","The plan's actual design (value always 1 per (kind,name)) is stricter than ESLint and avoids the same-count-swap blind spot — a strength the current framing obscures."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword to: 'Baseline keyed per (kind, name) with a fixed value of 1 — set membership, not a scalar count. This is deliberately STRICTER than ESLint's eslint-suppressions.json, which records a scalar count per (file, rule) bucket and thereby admits a same-count-swap blind spot (eslint/eslint#21226); keying per (kind, name) closes